-- Fermat's theorem on sums of two squares: a prime p ≡ 1 modulo 4 is a
-- sum of two squares, by the first supplement and Thue's lemma; an odd
-- prime is a sum of two squares exactly when it is 1 modulo 4.
-- Part of Cumulus, the Grace17 mathematics library.
-- Copyright (c) 2026 Grant Passmore.
